Description: Fix C++23 incomplete type error with std::unique_ptr<ScopedVABuffer> class members
 C++23 with libc++ introduced strict static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) >= 0) in
 std::unique_ptr destructor. When a class has a member variable of type
 std::unique_ptr<T> where T is only forward-declared (incomplete type),
 the compiler requires the complete type definition.
 .
 This fix includes the complete header for ScopedVABuffer instead of using
 a forward declaration, providing the complete type for std::unique_ptr
 class members in EncodeResult and EncodeJob classes.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-27

